cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research, please cite this archived version."
title: "Consecutive sum-freeness forces flat breaking"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "For binary vector functions, simultaneous (k-1)- and k-th order sum-freeness forces the affine span of every k-flat image to have dimension at least k+1. This answers Open Problem 3 of Rodríguez-Aldama, Šehović, Pasalic, and Kudin. The proof uses the quotient of the hyperplane-sum linear map by the total flat sum and includes equality examples."
